{
	"_source": "Captured from the theme-based code before the old theme code are removed: a temporary GUT test built the sunset, dawn, night and storm themes, ran the theme-to-cycle migration adapter, CloudSea.set_cycle_appearance(sunset, night, 0.6, (0.3,0.8,0.2)) and apply_storm_tint(sunset, storm, 0.5, blended sky) on a 2-clump sea, and recorded the puff-material uniforms; frames are the field-by-field tick/storm frames the old test built from the theme materials; occlusion comes from CloudSea.configure(sunset, 1.0, null, 1). Colours are [r,g,b,a], Vector3 [x,y,z], {v2}/{v4} Vector2/Vector4, '@texture' a Texture2D. JSON text keeps about 15 digits, so tests compare to 1e-5. Revised for the fixed sky quirks: the storm no longer re-copies the shared sky set, so snapshot_shared, blended_shared and the storm proc_zenith_color are gone (the far-fade gradient is checked against the frame).",
